      "ts": 1795667445000,
      "fullText": "EXCLUSIVE Technology EXCLUSIVE Xpeng Says Its Humanoid Robot Will Cost the Same as an EV Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift Expand The XPeng Inc. IRON humanoid robot interacts with an attendee at the company’s AI Day event in Guangzhou, China on Nov. 25. Photographer: Andrea Verdelli/Bloomberg Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift Gift this article Contact us: Provide news feedback or report an error Confidential tip? Send a tip to our reporters Site feedback: Take our Survey New Window Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift By Bloomberg News November 26, 2026 at 4:30 AM UTC Bookmark Save Takeaways by Bloomberg AI Xpeng Inc. ’s humanoid robots will cost roughly the same as an electric vehicle when they go on sale to the public in the second quarter. The IRON robot will be trained as a retail assistant in the first quarter, before going on sale, Xpeng Vice-Chairman Brian Gu said in an interview on Bloomberg TV Thursday. They could be priced around the median selling price for an EV, he said, without providing further details. The carmaker’s vehicles retail for around 119,800 yuan ($18,000) to 309,800 yuan."
